  "name": "OSMOLALITY-URINE",
  "code": "OSM UR",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>A urine osmolality test is a diagnostic test that measures the concentration of particles, such as electrolytes and minerals, in the urine. Here's an interpretation of urine osmolality test results:<br></p><ul><li>Low: A low result indicates that the urine is dilute and has a low concentration of particles. This may be caused by overhydration, such as drinking excessive amounts of water, or by kidney dysfunction, such as diabetes insipidus. Further evaluation may be necessary.</li><li>Normal: A normal result indicates that the urine has a normal concentration of particles. This is a normal result and indicates that the kidneys are functioning properly and that there is no significant dysfunction.</li><li>High: A high result indicates that the urine is concentrated and has a high concentration of particles. This may be caused by dehydration, such as from inadequate fluid intake or excessive sweating, or by kidney dysfunction, such as from kidney disease or certain medications.</li></ul>",
